    "definition": "Total receipts minus total outlays for a period. A negative number is a deficit (spending exceeded collections); a positive number is a surplus. This is a balancing figure, not a spending category — it is what financing (new borrowing) must cover. Reported for the month and cumulatively for the fiscal year to date.",
